  "relationship_graph_md": "```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  chat_engine --> primary_model\n  chat_engine --> mcp_tool --> external_mcp_server\n  chat_engine --> create_note --> clinical_db\n  chat_engine --> get_relevant_literature --> documents_db\n  phi_sanitization -. protects .-> pubmed_search\n  phi_sanitization -. protects .-> wiki_search\n  phi_sanitization -. protects .-> mcp_tool\n  proxy_auth -. protects .-> chat_endpoint\n```\n\nThe ChatEngine agent tool-calls into ~10 built-in tools plus any dynamically-registered external MCP server tools. Patient-record tools read/write the SQLCipher-encrypted clinical database; the literature tool reads the separate, unencrypted RAG vector store. External-facing tools (PubMed, Wikipedia, MCP) are PHI-sanitized before any request leaves the process. Auth is opt-in: proxy-header auth for Docker deployments (off by default) and a local bearer token for desktop builds only."
